---
const rows = [
  { subset: "FD001", baseline: 28.32, xgboost: 13.61, cnn: 13.64 },
  { subset: "FD002", baseline: 33.04, xgboost: 21.67, cnn: 21.62 },
  { subset: "FD003", baseline: 34.48, xgboost: 13.86, cnn: 18.09 },
  { subset: "FD004", baseline: 47.32, xgboost: 24.37, cnn: 25.08 },
];
const max = 50;
---

<figure class="metric-figure" aria-labelledby="metric-title metric-caption">
  <div class="figure-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Endpoint evaluation</p><h2 id="metric-title">Lower error, without complexity for its own sake.</h2></div>
    <p>Mean absolute error at the final observed cycle of each unseen test engine. Lower is better.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="bar-legend" aria-hidden="true"><span class="legend-baseline">Lifecycle</span><span class="legend-xgb">XGBoost</span><span class="legend-cnn">1D CNN</span></div>
  <div class="bar-grid" aria-hidden="true">
    {rows.map((row) => (
      <div class="bar-group">
        <strong>{row.subset}</strong>
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar baseline" style={`width:${(row.baseline / max) * 100}%`}></span><small>{row.baseline}</small></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar xgb" style={`width:${(row.xgboost / max) * 100}%`}></span><small>{row.xgboost}</small></div>
        <div class="bar-row"><span class="bar cnn" style={`width:${(row.cnn / max) * 100}%`}></span><small>{row.cnn}</small></div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <caption class="sr-only">Endpoint remaining useful life mean absolute error in cycles</caption>
      <thead><tr><th>Subset</th><th>Lifecycle</th><th>XGBoost</th><th>1D CNN</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>{rows.map((row) => <tr><th>{row.subset}</th><td>{row.baseline}</td><td>{row.xgboost}</td><td>{row.cnn}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <figcaption id="metric-caption">Models were trained independently per subset. The 1D CNN was effectively tied on FD001/FD002 and worse on FD003/FD004.</figcaption>
</figure>
